<section id="Ptx1" class="ltx_part">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_part">Supplementary Material</h2>

<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Theoretical Analysis</h3>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide the expressive guarantee of Low-Rank Adaption for transformer model with <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm Softmax}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm Softmax}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, we identify the conditions for the existence of low-rank adapters.
We summarize our main findings in the following informal theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Informal)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> be the frozen model and <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math> be the target model.
Under certain non-singularity assumption and LoRA-rank conditions, their exist low-rank adapters such that the adopted model <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> exactly equal to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The formal version is stated in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2 (Express capability of transformers). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.
Then we provide a detailed illustration.
We start with the definition of the target model <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and the adopted model <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Definition of target model <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and adopted model <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A1.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any input <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the dimension of token embedding and <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the number of tokens.
We consider a <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>-heads transformers <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm TF}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>TF</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm TF}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, consist of <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>-Transformer blocks and an output layer with parameter <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta=\left((W_{Ol}^{h},W_{Vl}^{h},W_{Kl}^{h},W_{Ql}^{h})_{h=1}^{H},W_{1l},W_{2l},b_{1l},b_{2l})_{l=1}^{L},W_{o}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta=\left((W_{Ol}^{h},W_{Vl}^{h},W_{Kl}^{h},W_{Ql}^{h})_{h=1}^{H},W_{1l},W_{2l},b_{1l},b_{2l})_{l=1}^{L},W_{o}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically, we formulate it as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Hidden layer:}\penalty\ \text{Attn}(Z_{l-1})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Hidden layer:</mtext><mtext>Attn</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Hidden layer:}\penalty\ \text{Attn}(Z_{l-1})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \sum_{h=1}^{H}\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h}\cdot\overline{Z}_{l-1}\cdot{\rm Softmax_{1}}(\overline{Z}_{l-1}^{\top}\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}\overline{Z}_{l-1})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \sum_{h=1}^{H}\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h}\cdot\overline{Z}_{l-1}\cdot{\rm Softmax_{1}}(\overline{Z}_{l-1}^{\top}\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}\overline{Z}_{l-1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{l}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{l}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ W_{2l}\cdot{\rm ReLU}(W_{1l}\cdot{\rm Attn}(Z_{l-1})+b_{1l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top})+b_{2l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>Attn</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ W_{2l}\cdot{\rm ReLU}(W_{1l}\cdot{\rm Attn}(Z_{l-1})+b_{1l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top})+b_{2l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm OutputLayer:}\penalty\ {\rm TF}_{\theta}(X)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>OutputLayer</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>TF</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm OutputLayer:}\penalty\ {\rm TF}_{\theta}(X)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ {\rm Softmax}_{1}(W_{o}Z_{L})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ {\rm Softmax}_{1}(W_{o}Z_{L}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we define <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{0}:=X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{0}:=X</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here, <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1l}^{h},W_{Vl}^{h},W_{Kl}^{h},W_{Ql}^{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1l}^{h},W_{Vl}^{h},W_{Kl}^{h},W_{Ql}^{h}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> are weight matrices in <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th attention layer.
Further, <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{1l},W_{2l}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{1l},W_{2l}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> are weight matrices and <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1l},b_{2l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1l},b_{2l}</annotation></semantics></math> are the bias vectors in the <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th feedforward layer.
Then we define the target model <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math> and the adopted model <math id="A1.Thmdefinition1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> are</p>
<table id="A1.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}:={\rm TF}_{\theta_{T}},\quad\theta_{T}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>TF</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}:={\rm TF}_{\theta_{T}},\quad\theta_{T}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \left((\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h},\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h},\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h},\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h})_{h=1}^{H},\overline{W}_{1l},\overline{W}_{2l},\overline{b}_{1l},\overline{b}_{2l})_{l=1}^{L},\overline{W}_{o}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0.500em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \left((\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h},\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h},\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h},\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h})_{h=1}^{H},\overline{W}_{1l},\overline{W}_{2l},\overline{b}_{1l},\overline{b}_{2l})_{l=1}^{L},\overline{W}_{o}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f:={\rm TF}_{\theta_{A}},\quad\theta_{A}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>:=</mo><msub><mi>TF</mi><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f:={\rm TF}_{\theta_{A}},\quad\theta_{A}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ ((W_{Ol}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ol}^{h},W_{Vl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Vl}^{h},W_{Kl}^{h}+\Delta W_{kl}^{h},W_{Ql}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})_{h=1}^{H}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ ((W_{Ol}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ol}^{h},W_{Vl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Vl}^{h},W_{Kl}^{h}+\Delta W_{kl}^{h},W_{Ql}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})_{h=1}^{H},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle W_{1l}+\Delta W_{1l},W_{2l}+\Delta W_{2l},\widehat{b}_{1l},\widehat{b}_{2l})_{l=1}^{L},W_{o}+\Delta W_{o})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle W_{1l}+\Delta W_{1l},W_{2l}+\Delta W_{2l},\widehat{b}_{1l},\widehat{b}_{2l})_{l=1}^{L},W_{o}+\Delta W_{o}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Moreover, we define the best low-rank approximation for matrix <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Best Low-rank Approximation for <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="A1.Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For any matrix <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the singular value decomposition (SVD) of <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> is expressed as <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=UDV^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=UDV^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Above <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U,V\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> are orthonormal matrices and <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> is a diagonal matrix.
Let the singular value of <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> are denoted as <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}(W)\geq\ldots\geq\sigma_{D}(W)\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}(W)\geq\ldots\geq\sigma_{D}(W)\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
When <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;D</annotation></semantics></math>,let <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{d}(W)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{d}(W)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any rank <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\rm LRA}_{r}(W):=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}(W)u_{i}v_{i}^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LRA</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>r</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\rm LRA}_{r}(W):=\sum_{i=1}^{r}\sigma_{i}(W)u_{i}v_{i}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i},v_{i}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i},v_{i}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> are the <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th column of <math id="A1.Thmdefinition2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U,V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U,V</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">According to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Eckart &amp; Young (1936)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mirsky (1960)</a></cite>, <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm LRA}_{r}(W)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>LRA</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm LRA}_{r}(W)</annotation></semantics></math> are the best rank-<math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> approximation in the Frobenius norm or the <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-norm of <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.
To present our results, we now introduce non-singularity assumption based on <a href="#A1.Thmdefinition2" title="Definition A.2 (Best Low-rank Approximation for 𝑊). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Non-Singularity)<span id="A1.Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a fixed <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in[D]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in[D]</annotation></semantics></math>, the weight matrices of both the target model, the frozen model and the following matrices are non-singular, for all <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in[R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in[R]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Specifically,</p>
<table id="A1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ W_{Kl}^{h\top}W_{Ql}^{h}+{\rm LRA}_{r}(\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}-W_{Kl}^{h\top}W_{Ql}^{h}),\text{ for all }h\in[H]\text{ and }l=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LRA</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> and </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ W_{Kl}^{h\top}W_{Ql}^{h}+{\rm LRA}_{r}(\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}-W_{Kl}^{h\top}W_{Ql}^{h}),\text{ for all }h\in[H]\text{ and }l=1,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
