<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ W_{o}W_{2L}+{\rm LRA}_{r}(\overline{W}_{o}\overline{W}_{2L}-W_{o}W_{2L})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LRA</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ W_{o}W_{2L}+{\rm LRA}_{r}(\overline{W}_{o}\overline{W}_{2L}-W_{o}W_{2L}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">are non-singular, where <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\rm LRA}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LRA</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\rm LRA}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the rank-<math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> approximation follows <a href="#A1.Thmdefinition2" title="Definition A.2 (Best Low-rank Approximation for 𝑊). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Definition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Under a non-singularity assumption (<a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1 (Non-Singularity). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>), we apply another helper lemma from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zeng &amp; Lee (2024)</a></cite> to construct the weight matrices in <a href="#A1.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem A.2 (Express capability of transformers). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Exactly represent target model, Lemma 7 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zeng &amp; Lee (2024)</a></cite>)<span id="A1.Thmlemma1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Define error matrix <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E:=\overline{W}-\prod_{l=1}^{L}W_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E:=\overline{W}-\prod_{l=1}^{L}W_{l}</annotation></semantics></math>, and denote its rank by <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{E}=\operatorname{rank}(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{E}=\operatorname{rank}(E)</annotation></semantics></math>. For a given LoRA-rank <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in[D]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in[D]</annotation></semantics></math>, assume that all the weight matrices of the frozen model <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(W_{l}\right)_{l=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(W_{l}\right)_{l=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{l=1}^{L}W_{l}+\mathrm{LRA}_{r}(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LRA</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{l=1}^{L}W_{l}+\mathrm{LRA}_{r}(E)</annotation></semantics></math> are non-singular for all <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq R(L-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq R(L-1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, the approximation error</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\min_{\Delta W_{l}:\operatorname{rank}\left(\Delta W_{l}\right)\leq R}\left\|\prod_{l=1}^{L}\left(W_{l}+\Delta W_{l}\right)-\overline{W}\right\|_{2}=\sigma_{RL+1}\underbrace{\left(\overline{W}-\prod_{l=1}^{L}W_{l}\right)}_{\text{Error matrix }E}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mtext>Error matrix </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\Delta W_{l}:\operatorname{rank}\left(\Delta W_{l}\right)\leq R}\left\|\prod_{l=1}^{L}\left(W_{l}+\Delta W_{l}\right)-\overline{W}\right\|_{2}=\sigma_{RL+1}\underbrace{\left(\overline{W}-\prod_{l=1}^{L}W_{l}\right)}_{\text{Error matrix }E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and the optimal solution to the matrix approximation problem satisfies <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{l=1}^{L}\left(W_{l}+\Delta W_{l}\right)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{l=1}^{L}\left(W_{l}+\Delta W_{l}\right)=</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{l=1}^{L}W_{l}+\mathrm{LRA}_{RL\wedge R_{E}}(E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LRA</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{l=1}^{L}W_{l}+\mathrm{LRA}_{RL\wedge R_{E}}(E)</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, when <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\geq\left\lceil\frac{R_{E}}{L}\right\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mo>⌈</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo>⌉</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\geq\left\lceil\frac{R_{E}}{L}\right\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{l=1}^{L}\left(W_{l}+\Delta W_{l}\right)=\overline{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{l=1}^{L}\left(W_{l}+\Delta W_{l}\right)=\overline{W}</annotation></semantics></math>, implying <math id="A1.Thmlemma1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\equiv\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\equiv\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">With <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1 (Non-Singularity). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> and <a href="#A1.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma A.1 (Exactly represent target model, Lemma 7 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we show that for any input <math id="A1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>, their exist a adapted model <math id="A1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> capable of approximating target model <math id="A1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math> exactly, i.e, <math id="A1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)=\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)=\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem A.2</span></span><span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Express capability of transformers)<span id="A1.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose LoRA-rank <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\in[D]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\in[D]</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1 (Non-Singularity). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> hold.
Define the rank-based
functionality gap <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to i-th Outlier-Efficient Hopfield block <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i\in[L])" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i\in[L])</annotation></semantics></math> or output layer <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i=L+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i=L+1)</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G_{i}=\begin{cases}\max_{h}({\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{Ki}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Qi}^{h}-W_{Ki}^{h\top}W_{Qi}^{h}))\vee\max_{h}({\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{1i}\overline{W}_{Oi}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vi}^{h}-W_{1i}W_{Oi}^{h}W_{Vi}^{h})),&amp;i=1,\\
\max_{h}({\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{2,i-1}^{\top}\overline{W}_{Ki}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Qi}^{h}\overline{W}_{2,i-1}-W_{2,i-1}^{\top}W_{Ki}^{h\top}W_{Qi}^{h}W_{2,i-1}),\\
\vee\max_{h}({\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{1i}\overline{W}_{Oi}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vi}^{h}\overline{W}_{2,i-1}-W_{1i}W_{Oi}^{h}W_{Vi}^{h}W_{2,i-1})),&amp;2\leq i\leq L,\\
{\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{o}\overline{W}_{2L}-W_{o}W_{2L}),&amp;i=L+1.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>max</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>rank</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msup><mi>W</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>rank</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G_{i}=\begin{cases}\max_{h}({\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{Ki}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Qi}^{h}-W_{Ki}^{h\top}W_{Qi}^{h}))\vee\max_{h}({\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{1i}\overline{W}_{Oi}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vi}^{h}-W_{1i}W_{Oi}^{h}W_{Vi}^{h})),&amp;i=1,\\
\max_{h}({\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{2,i-1}^{\top}\overline{W}_{Ki}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Qi}^{h}\overline{W}_{2,i-1}-W_{2,i-1}^{\top}W_{Ki}^{h\top}W_{Qi}^{h}W_{2,i-1}),\\
\vee\max_{h}({\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{1i}\overline{W}_{Oi}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vi}^{h}\overline{W}_{2,i-1}-W_{1i}W_{Oi}^{h}W_{Vi}^{h}W_{2,i-1})),&amp;2\leq i\leq L,\\
{\rm rank}(\overline{W}_{o}\overline{W}_{2L}-W_{o}W_{2L}),&amp;i=L+1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\geq\max_{i\in[L+1]}\lceil\frac{G_{i}}{2}\rceil" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌈</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌉</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\geq\max_{i\in[L+1]}\lceil\frac{G_{i}}{2}\rceil</annotation></semantics></math>, then there exists low-rank adapters with rank lower than <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((\Delta W_{Kl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ql}^{h},\Delta W_{Vl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ol}^{h})_{h=1}^{H})_{l=1}^{L},\Delta W_{2L},\Delta W_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((\Delta W_{Kl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ql}^{h},\Delta W_{Vl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ol}^{h})_{h=1}^{H})_{l=1}^{L},\Delta W_{2L},\Delta W_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> with other low-rank adapters set to <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>, and updated bias vectors <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\widehat{b}_{1l},\widehat{b}_{2l})_{l=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\widehat{b}_{1l},\widehat{b}_{2l})_{l=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, such that for any input <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times N}</annotation></semantics></math>, the adapted model <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> exactly approximates target model <math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,
<math id="A1.Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(X)=\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(X)=\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We build our proof on <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zeng &amp; Lee (2024)</a></cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we ensure that, for each Outlier-Efficient Hopfield block, the output from the first feedforward layer in the target model matches that in the adapted model.
Then, we select an appropriate output layer weight matrix to complete the proof.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We define <math id="A1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{H}_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{H}_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times N}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Z}_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Z}_{l}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times N}</annotation></semantics></math> as the intermediate and final outputs of the <math id="A1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th transformer block in the target model <math id="A1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, respectively.
For any <math id="A1.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>, they are formulated as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{H}_{l}:=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{H}_{l}:=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ {\rm ReLU}(\overline{W}_{1l}(\sum_{h=1}^{H}\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h}\cdot\overline{Z}_{l-1}\cdot{\rm Softmax_{1}}(\overline{Z}_{l-1}^{\top}\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}\overline{Z}_{l-1}))+\overline{b}_{1l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ {\rm ReLU}(\overline{W}_{1l}(\sum_{h=1}^{H}\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h}\cdot\overline{Z}_{l-1}\cdot{\rm Softmax_{1}}(\overline{Z}_{l-1}^{\top}\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}\overline{Z}_{l-1}))+\overline{b}_{1l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{Z}_{l}:=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{Z}_{l}:=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \overline{W}_{2l}\overline{H}_{l}+\overline{b}_{2l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \overline{W}_{2l}\overline{H}_{l}+\overline{b}_{2l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Correspondingly, we introduce <math id="A1.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{Z}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{Z}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the intermediate output of the first feedforward layer and the final output of the <math id="A1.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th Outlier-Efficient Hopfield block for the adapted model <math id="A1.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{H}_{l}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{H}_{l}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ {\rm ReLU}(W_{1l}(\sum_{h=1}^{H}(W_{Ol}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ol}^{h})(W_{Vl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Vl}^{h})\cdot\widehat{Z}_{l-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ReLU</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ {\rm ReLU}(W_{1l}(\sum_{h=1}^{H}(W_{Ol}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ol}^{h})(W_{Vl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Vl}^{h})\cdot\widehat{Z}_{l-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\cdot{\rm Softmax_{1}}(\widehat{Z}_{l-1}^{\top}(W_{Kl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Kl}^{h})^{\top}(W_{Ql}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})\widehat{Z}_{l1})+\widehat{b}_{1l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>Softmax</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\cdot{\rm Softmax_{1}}(\widehat{Z}_{l-1}^{\top}(W_{Kl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Kl}^{h})^{\top}(W_{Ql}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})\widehat{Z}_{l1})+\widehat{b}_{1l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{Z}_{l}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{Z}_{l}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ W_{2l}\widehat{H}_{l}+\widehat{b}_{2l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ W_{2l}\widehat{H}_{l}+\widehat{b}_{2l}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">for any <math id="A1.p9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="A1.p9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{Z}_{0}=\widehat{Z}_{0}=X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{Z}_{0}=\widehat{Z}_{0}=X</annotation></semantics></math>.
Next, we inductively construct the adapter weight matrices
<math id="A1.p9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="((\Delta W_{Ol}^{h},\Delta W_{Vl}^{h},\Delta W_{Kl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})_{h=1}^{H},\widehat{b}_{1l},\widehat{b}_{2l})_{l=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">((\Delta W_{Ol}^{h},\Delta W_{Vl}^{h},\Delta W_{Kl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})_{h=1}^{H},\widehat{b}_{1l},\widehat{b}_{2l})_{l=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.p9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then select the low-rank adapters for <math id="A1.p9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2L}</annotation></semantics></math> and the <math id="A1.p9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> to approximate the output of the target model.
For unmentioned low-rank adapters, we set them as <math id="A1.p9.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">When <math id="A1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.p10.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">  To achieve <math id="A1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, the following conditions must be satisfied:</span></span></p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1em;">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Bias Vector: <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{b}_{1l}=\overline{b}_{1l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{b}_{1l}=\overline{b}_{1l}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Query and Key: <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{Kl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Kl}^{h})^{\top}(W_{Ql}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})=\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{Kl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Kl}^{h})^{\top}(W_{Ql}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})=\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Value and First Feedforward Layer:
<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{Ol}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ol}^{h})(W_{Vl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Vl}^{h})=W_{1l}^{-1}\overline{W}_{1l}\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{Ol}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ol}^{h})(W_{Vl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Vl}^{h})=W_{1l}^{-1}\overline{W}_{1l}\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">It is simple to check that we only need to set <math id="A1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{b}_{1l}=\overline{b}_{1l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{b}_{1l}=\overline{b}_{1l}</annotation></semantics></math> to, and select rank-<math id="A1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> or lower matrices
<math id="A1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{Kl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ql}^{h},\Delta W_{Ol}^{h},\Delta W_{Vl}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{Kl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ql}^{h},\Delta W_{Ol}^{h},\Delta W_{Vl}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> as suggested by <a href="#A1.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma A.1 (Exactly represent target model, Lemma 7 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
This ensures <math id="A1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">When <math id="A1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A1.p12.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">  For the cases <math id="A1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=2,\ldots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=2,\ldots,L</annotation></semantics></math>,
we assume the induction hypothesis holds for <math id="A1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l-1</annotation></semantics></math>, which is <math id="A1.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{l-1}=\overline{H}_{l-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{l-1}=\overline{H}_{l-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We let <math id="A1.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{b}_{2,l-1}=W_{2,l-1}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}^{-1}\overline{b}_{2,l-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{b}_{2,l-1}=W_{2,l-1}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}^{-1}\overline{b}_{2,l-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, then it holds,</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\widehat{Z}_{l-1}=W_{2,l-1}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}^{-1}\overline{Z}_{l-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\widehat{Z}_{l-1}=W_{2,l-1}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}^{-1}\overline{Z}_{l-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting (<a href="#A1.E3" title="Equation A.3 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.3</span></a>) into (<a href="#A1.E1" title="Equation A.1 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>) and (<a href="#A1.E2" title="Equation A.2 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>),
the necessary conditions become:</span></p>
<ul id="A1.I2" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1em;">
<li id="A1.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Bias Vector: <math id="A1.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{b}_{1l}=\overline{b}_{1l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{b}_{1l}=\overline{b}_{1l}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Query and Key: <math id="A1.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{Kl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Kl}^{h})^{\top}(W_{Ql}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})=W_{2,l-1}^{-1\top}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}^{\top}\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}W_{2,l-1}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{Kl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Kl}^{h})^{\top}(W_{Ql}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ql}^{h})=W_{2,l-1}^{-1\top}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}^{\top}\overline{W}_{Kl}^{h\top}\overline{W}_{Ql}^{h}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}W_{2,l-1}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Value and Output Projection:
<math id="A1.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(W_{Ol}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ol}^{h})(W_{Vl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Vl}^{h})=W_{1l}^{-1}\overline{W}_{1l}\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}W_{2,l-1}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(W_{Ol}^{h}+\Delta W_{Ol}^{h})(W_{Vl}^{h}+\Delta W_{Vl}^{h})=W_{1l}^{-1}\overline{W}_{1l}\overline{W}_{Ol}^{h}\overline{W}_{Vl}^{h}\overline{W}_{2,l-1}W_{2,l-1}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">By setting <math id="A1.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{b}_{1l}=\overline{b}_{1l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{b}_{1l}=\overline{b}_{1l}</annotation></semantics></math> and adjusting <math id="A1.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{Kl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ql}^{h},\Delta W_{Ol}^{h},\Delta W_{Vl}^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow><mi>h</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{Kl}^{h},\Delta W_{Ql}^{h},\Delta W_{Ol}^{h},\Delta W_{Vl}^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in[H]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in[H]</annotation></semantics></math> based on <a href="#A1.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma A.1 (Exactly represent target model, Lemma 7 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we satisfy all three conditions above, thereby obtaining <math id="A1.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A1.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[L]\backslash\{1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[L]\backslash\{1\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output Layer Analysis.<span id="A1.p13.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
By applying the induction method, we have established <math id="A1.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{H}_{l}=\overline{H}_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>.
We only need to select appropriate weight matrices to ensure that <math id="A1.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)=f(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)=f(X)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A1.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The final output of the target model <math id="A1.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}</annotation></semantics></math> with input <math id="A1.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)=\text{Softmax}_{1}(\overline{W}_{o}\overline{Z}_{L})=\text{Softmax}_{1}(\overline{W}_{o}(\overline{W}_{2L}\overline{H}_{L}+\overline{b}_{2L}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Softmax</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Softmax</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)=\text{Softmax}_{1}(\overline{W}_{o}\overline{Z}_{L})=\text{Softmax}_{1}(\overline{W}_{o}(\overline{W}_{2L}\overline{H}_{L}+\overline{b}_{2L}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, the final output of the adapted model <math id="A1.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> with input <math id="A1.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math> can be written as</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(X)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(X)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \text{Softmax}_{1}((W_{o}+\Delta W_{o})\widehat{Z}_{L})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Softmax</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Z</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \text{Softmax}_{1}((W_{o}+\Delta W_{o})\widehat{Z}_{L})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\penalty\ \text{Softmax}_{1}((W_{o}+\Delta W_{o})((W_{2L}\Delta W_{2L})\widehat{H}_{L}+\widehat{b}_{2L}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Softmax</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\penalty\ \text{Softmax}_{1}((W_{o}+\Delta W_{o})((W_{2L}\Delta W_{2L})\widehat{H}_{L}+\widehat{b}_{2L}\mathbf{1}_{N}^{\top})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">To achieve <math id="A1.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)=f(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext class="undefined">\macc@depth</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@set@skewchar</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext class="undefined">\macc@nested@a</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>111</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\macc@depth\char 1\relax\macc@set@skewchar\macc@nested@a 111{f}(X)=f(X)</annotation></semantics></math>, we select <math id="A1.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{2L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta W_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta W_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> based on <a href="#A1.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma A.1 (Exactly represent target model, Lemma 7 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, and let <math id="A1.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{b}_{2L}=(W_{o}+\Delta W_{o})^{-1}\overline{W}_{o}\overline{b}_{2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{b}_{2L}=(W_{o}+\Delta W_{o})^{-1}\overline{W}_{o}\overline{b}_{2L}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{o}+\Delta W_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{o}+\Delta W_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> is invertible as shown in the proof of <a href="#A1.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma A.1 (Exactly represent target model, Lemma 7 of ( ) ). ‣ Appendix A Theoretical Analysis ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>.
Combining above, we complete the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Computational Resource</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We perform all experiments using 2 NVIDIA A100 GPU with 80GB of memory and a 24-core Intel(R) Xeon(R) Gold 6338 CPU operating at 2.00GHz.
Our code is developed in PyTorch and utilizes the Hugging Face Transformer Library for experimental execution.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Hyperparameters</h4>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We present the hyperparameters used in the fine-tuning stage for each model.
We use <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AdamW</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov &amp; Hutter, 2019</a>)</cite> as the optimizer.
Most of the other hyperparameters remain the same across all models and datasets, including a batch size of 32, a warmup step of 50, and a weight decay of 0.01.
A learning rate of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3e^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3e^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> is used for all models during fine-tuning.
For low-rank adaptation, we use a learning rate of <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1e^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1e^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>, with a LoRA rank of 8 and LoRA alpha set to 16. For each task, we use different training steps as shown in <a href="#A2.T5" title="In B.2 Hyperparameters ‣ Appendix B Experimental Setup ‣ Supplementary Material ‣ Fast and Low-Cost Genomic Foundation Models via Outlier Removal" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.
During pre-training, the model is trained for 200,000 steps with a batch size of 1024 and a maximum sequence length of 512, using the AdamW optimizer with <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.98" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.98</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.98</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=1e^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=1e^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The pre-training stage takes approximately 4 days using 2 NVIDIA A100 80G GPUs.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 5</span>: </span><span id="A2.T5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">The number of training steps.<span id="A2.T5.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We present the number of training steps we use in our experiments. In the task of Transcription Factor Prediction on the Mouse genome,
we train the model for 1000 steps on each dataset.</span></span></figcaption>
