<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>All Results in Low-rank Adaptation</h4>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we present a comprehensive evaluation of various models under different low-rank adaptation (LoRA) strategies. The experiments compare DNABERT-2, <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Germ-T</span>, and <span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Germ</span> models across multiple biological prediction tasks, including epigenetic marks prediction, promoter detection, and transcription factor prediction in both human and mouse datasets. The adaptation methods assessed include Full Fine-tuning, LoRA, QLoRA, and LoftQ.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T8" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A4.T8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 8</span>: </span><span id="A4.T8.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Performance Comparison of Full Fine-tuning with DNABERT-2.<span id="A4.T8.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> This table shows the performance of all models on the full fine-tuning task.</span></span></figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
